From cbcd2874c43cffc7b48831543c38df98216909d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 00:20:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] ui: read button and toggle radius from the Zeo token

Converts the directly-styled controls, where the chokepoint converted the
inherited ones. Buttons hold at the control step (6px) and no higher -- a 10px
button in a code editor reads "web app in a window". The per-corner form stays:
it is what leaves a button group's inner edges square so the group reads as one
control, and GPUI's per-corner setters take a Pixels like every other radius
setter, so the plain token covers it with no per-corner token API.

Each control takes the step its role calls for rather than one blanket value:
the checkbox stays at 4px, and the switch's track, thumb and placeholder dot stay
full -- a switch is a pill and its knob is a circle. The visual step is
unchanged; what changes is that it now comes from the token.

The coverage grep alone could not have caught a mistake here -- it proves the
literals are gone, never that the right step arrived, and it is blind to the
per-corner forms entirely. The tests assert against the token's resolved value at
two ui_font_size values AND at a non-default zeo.radius_scale: GPUI's rounded_*
literals are rem-based and so already track ui_font_size, which makes
radius_scale the only lever that can tell a token from the literal it replaced.

Covers R2.7, R1.2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
